# Local build caches left behind after the macOS/Android app surfaces were
# dropped. Their tracked trees are gone from the index, but the caches stay
# on disk, so without these rules the change-impact governance scan sees them
# as unowned changed files and fails the owner.
apps/macos/.build/
apps/shared/

# Generated protocol schema (produced via pnpm protocol:gen)
dist/protocol.schema.json
.ant-colony/

# Local runtime state written by operator scripts and runners (branches/_system)
branches/_system/

# Scratch space created at runtime by operator scripts
tmp/

# Generated extension declaration output
ops/external-channel-artifacts/promotions/

# Eclipse
**/.project
**/.classpath
**/.settings/
**/.gradle/

# Synthing
**/.stfolder/
# Keeps generated output, local credentials, caches, and runtime state out of git.
tmp-lcx-owner-dashboard*.png

# Runtime state and test scratch left at the repository root. The default finance
# state directory and the local-brain eval verification output are written here by
# operator runs, and the path-alias suites create their sandbox directories here.
# They are untracked by design, but without these rules the change-impact
# governance scan reads them as unowned changed files and fails the owner.
/state/
/openclaw-path-alias-*/
src/canvas-host/a2ui/test-link-*.txt
# Scratch directories a local-brain planning run leaves behind. Same reason as
# above: unowned changed files would fail the change-impact owner scan.
/tmp-lcx-local-brain-plan-*/

# Read-only probe scripts. They must live inside the repository (running them from
# /tmp fails with ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED, because tsx cannot resolve the
# exports of @mariozechner/* from outside the tree) and they are deleted once the
# question they answer is answered. That in-tree placement is driven by module
# resolution, not by governance, so a probe that is still in use would otherwise
# fail the change-impact scan for a reason that has nothing to do with ownership.
/.lcx-probe/
